  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lockheed Martin has $10B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, from 140 awards with an average award size of $71.8M. Obligations are down 3.6% year over year. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market, accounting for $9.2B of current-year obligations. Historical fiscal-year obligations rose from $4.7B in FY21 to $8.7B in FY23, then moved to $7.3B in FY24 and $10.4B in FY25 before reaching $10B in FY26. The current-year totals are partial, and the figures cited are contract obligations except for award-value tables noted elsewhere. Other active NAICS markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $635M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $62.7M, and several smaller categories including Engineering Services at $20.2M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $40.3M. This snapshot highlights concentration in missile and space vehicle work and a small number of very large awards driving total obligations.",
